<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύζομαι</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		, used mostly in pres.: impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκύζοντο, σκύζοντο</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Q.S.
			3.133
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			5.338
		</span></i>: 
			Ep.
		
		aor. opt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύσσαιτο </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπι-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			7.306
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be angry
				with</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυζομένη Διὶ πατρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύζεσθαί οἱ εἰπὲ θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.113
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μοι σκύζευ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.209
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to be wroth</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ σευ ἔγωγε σκυζομένης ἀλέγω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.483
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9.198
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυδ-μαίνω</span> and prob.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυθρός</span>.)</div>
